You are starting to construct the arguments for
why there could be an Alchemist class in NetHack.
I'm sure this one has been around the barn a few
times, but bear with me, I have improved game
balance in my sights. [Right!]

By giving it the starting success rate of the
historical alchemists (or worse, if someone can
invent "worse" than frequent mercury fume
poisoning and various nasty gagging or explosive
deaths) and letting it slowly work up from "almost
every attempt fails and usually produces something
inferior to the least of the ingredients,
instadeath occasionally among them" to
creating gold about the time gold is PC-burdening
litter and not a desirable good, and also having
recipes requiring multiple ingredients not easily
found together ("tin of newt", "corpse of bat",
"eye of floating", "crystal of warp", "leaf of
'leave, lupe!'") and bewilderingly described
("contain he who breeds under moist rocks in an
armor of tin") or just silly ("in a dented pot,
with a copper stirring implement, beneath a
waxing gibbous moon, while circling deosil,
mix..."): you get the idea, one could keep it in
balance while holding out the rare chance of
success giving a fabulous reward ("your
incantation produces a glistening slivery potion,
could this be the fabled 'make reflective'?", "you
seem to have invented an inky black gloop probably
only suitable for an easily refillable marker,
those ones made from mummified arch-lich fingers
by recipe 218 in volume 3", "the ball of molton
metal suddenly clarifies; you think you see an
image within it; could that be Dad?  'No, Dad, not
my plump succulent pet pig Porky! I can eat _lots_
more grass without complaining again until harvest
time, or Sis coming back with some canned goods, I
promise!' your baby sister seems to be wailing,
the insufferable brat who wouldn't contribute  a
zorkmid to your going away 'buy Suzy unrotted
armor' fund but now expects you to bring home
replacement bacon.  The image fades as the ball
cools, do you have more coal oil for your brazier,
or should we just let Porky roast, the little
night-before-prom dress-munching squealer who made
you a laughing stock and the only deb in a flour
sack?(*)" "z - a chaotic ball of DV (distant-vision)
with kolour-klear and full surround stereo in
attractive decorator veneer") attainable no other
way.

[Okay, that last might be a bit over the top...]

The main motivation being of course to move all
other kinds of alchemy under this infuriating
system and out of reach of other classes except
with deep and infrequently successful
subspecialization, to remove one of the "wimp-out
NH upgraded" reasons Ghennom seems to bore people
with infinite resources and no perceptible reason
to worry.

It isn't that ascensions are too frequent for
_me_, just for other players, and Something Must
Be Done.

This would leave room for endless efforts by
programming deviants with sadistic imaginations
to implement another impossible alchemical spell.

Only a thought, don't all throw your spoiled
fruit at once.

